Tom Sorensen (gt0040a@prism.gatech.EDU) wrote:
: The only thing I don't like about this is that it uses up a prayer counter...
: bad. Given the new hunger rules I'm usually using my prayers to keep from
: dying of starvation...

: Another question regarding this- does it make a difference if a Chaotic or
: Neutral character prays at a Lawful altar to get holy water? If so then this
: really stinks, since holy water is so useful (although this may reduce the
: amount of abuse).

You should only pray at your own altar.  Your god wouldn't like it if you
did.  But ANY altar can produce holy water.

: Otherwise I like this feature- it lets you ID the water so you don't have
: to go searching for a lawful altar all the time. As long as you have 1 potion
: of holy water you can always generate more.

Here are some of my favorite ways of getting holy water:
MINOR SPOLIERS

- Get all of the useless potions you can together in a pile.  Also include
  all useless scrolls and spellbooks.
- Then zap all of them with a wand of cancellation.

-or- 

- Find a pool of water, or get a fountain to overflow.  Its better to use
  a pool because they don't dry up.
- Find some way to levitate over the pool.
- Dip the potions twice or the scrolls and spellbooks once to wipe them
out

Then get all of the potions to water to be in one inventory slot and
dip them into a potion of holy water.  Unfortuanately for blank scrolls
only one scroll can be written on at a time.  So the only reason to get
them into one directory slot is to save the total number of slots
used.

